00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.880
I talked yesterday, yesterday on the show
about this concept, stochastic terrorism.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.880
Okay.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:12.169
Stochastic terrorism once again is when through
media messages, through mass communication

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:18.490
methods, uh, if someone has a large enough
audience and they harp about the need to take

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:24.699
care of someone in the public eye or the need
to do something about a person or an organization,

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.990
it becomes statistically more and more likely
that someone in the audience will actually

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.760
be inspired to go and do something in the
real world as a result of those mass communication

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.000
messages that they've heard.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.300
Glenn Beck famously was constantly ranting
and raving about the tides foundation with

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.820
all sorts of conspiracies and eventually it
actually inspired someone in his audience

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.739
to go and try to do something about the tides
foundation.

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:51.300
Hopefully, if I recall the story correctly,
he was stopped by a police on his way to do

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.300
that thing.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.340
Now, of course, as as a current law, Glen
Beck cannot be found guilty in any way for

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.579
conspiring with that individual.

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:00.309
There is no actual connection.

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:05.070
It's through the mass messaging that that's
the castic terrorism is carried out.

